error[L0262]: cannot borrow `c` as mutable, as it is not declared as mutable (E0596)
  --> tests/corpus/reject/method_call_shapes.lc:27:5
   |
27 |     c.bump(); //~ error: L0262 cannot borrow `c` as mutable, as it is not declared as mutable (E0596)
   |     ^
   |
   = note: a `&mut` argument is rooted at a binding the call may assign: declare it `let mut c`, or as a parameter `mut c: T` or `c: &mut T`
error[L0261]: `Counter::get` takes `&self`, and the receiver is not a place the call could lend
  --> tests/corpus/reject/method_call_shapes.lc:32:5
   |
32 |     Counter::fresh().get() //~ error: L0261 `Counter::get` takes `&self`, and the receiver is not a place the call could lend
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = note: a reference lasts for one call and lends a place the caller holds, `x` or `x.f`; bind the value with `let` first
error[L0207]: `Counter::fresh` takes no `self`, and is called as `Counter::fresh(..)`
  --> tests/corpus/reject/method_call_shapes.lc:36:7
   |
36 |     c.fresh() //~ error: L0207 `Counter::fresh` takes no `self`, and is called as `Counter::fresh(..)`
   |       ^^^^^
   |
   = note: a function of an `impl` block without a `self` parameter is an associated function, named by its type, as in Rust
error[L0207]: no method named `size` found for `Counter` (E0599)
  --> tests/corpus/reject/method_call_shapes.lc:40:7
   |
40 |     c.size() //~ error: L0207 no method named `size` found for `Counter` (E0599)
   |       ^^^^
   |
   = note: a method is declared in `impl Counter { .. }` with `self`, `&self`, or `&mut self` as its first parameter
error[L0204]: unknown function `get`
